hoice is clearly `pass: []`. This keeps me in the game, preserves my hand, and provides a good chance to win later.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: My hand relies heavily on structure (a 5-pair sequence 33-44-55-66-77 and high pairs KK, AA). Playing a single K or A would break these high pairs, leaving me with weak isolated singles and diminishing my hand\'s power. Playing the 2 on a Queen is inefficient and risky, as the Landlord likely holds higher cards (Jokers or other 2s) given the unknown cards.\n\nReason: By passing, I preserve the integrity of my pairs (KK, AA) and save my 2 for a more critical moment or to support a run later. It is not efficient to break a high pair to beat a medium card like a Queen, and my teammate may be better positioned to handle this single card.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
